  "howItWorksTitle": "How we calculate calories",
  "howItWorksTooltip": "How do we calculate calories?",
  "howItWorksIntro": "Most nutrition apps guess the portion from a single 2D photo. Calorii Fit actually measures the volume of the food on the plate, using your phone's depth map — that's why the estimate is more accurate.",
  "howItWorksStep1Title": "Photograph your plate",
  "howItWorksStep1Description": "A single photo, no special positioning.",
  "howItWorksStep2Title": "Your phone captures depth",
  "howItWorksStep2GenericDescription": "Your phone uses LiDAR, ARCore Depth, or a dual camera, depending on the model, to know how tall the food is, not just what it looks like from above.",
  "howItWorksStep3Title": "Claude identifies the foods",
  "howItWorksStep3Description": "The model recognizes what's on the plate and marks the approximate outline of each food item — it doesn't calculate calories itself, only identifies.",
  "howItWorksStep4Title": "Volume becomes grams, then calories",
  "howItWorksStep4Description": "The depth map × each food's outline gives a volume in cm³. A density table (specific to each type of food) converts the volume into grams, and the nutrition database converts the grams into calories and macronutrients.",
  "howItWorksStep5Title": "You confirm or correct",
  "howItWorksStep5Description": "The automatic estimate is never saved directly — you always see a confirmation screen where you can adjust the portion or change the identified food.",
  "howItWorksSeeDeviceMethod": "See which method your phone uses",
  "howItWorksDepthLidar": "Your phone has LiDAR — the most precise method available on a phone today, with a typical error of just 10-15%.",
  "howItWorksDepthArcore": "Your phone uses the ARCore Depth API to estimate scene depth.",
  "howItWorksDepthPortrait": "Your phone estimates depth from the dual camera (portrait mode) — less precise than LiDAR, but still better than a plain photo.",
  "howItWorksDepthReference": "Your phone has no depth sensor, so we use a plate's standard diameter as a scale reference — the least precise method, but still better than a purely visual guess.",
  "howItWorksDepthUnknown": "We couldn't determine the method your phone uses.",

